# Planted bugs for the lineage model. Each one must make the named check miss its expectation.
run fv-alloy lineage-pii.als
properties NoUnmaskedPIIAtASink_MaskingCoversLineage NoUnmaskedPIIAtASink_MaskingCoversDirectPIIOnly
file lineage-pii.als

mutation the lineage rule masks only the columns tagged PII and stops following transforms
detects NoUnmaskedPIIAtASink_MaskingCoversLineage
- pred MaskingCoversLineage {
-   all s: Sink, c: Column | (c in s.exposes and DerivedFromPII[c]) implies c in s.masked
- }
+ pred MaskingCoversLineage {
+   all s: Sink, c: Column | (c in s.exposes and c in PIIColumn) implies c in s.masked
+ }

mutation the direct-only rule is widened to cover lineage, so it no longer demonstrates the gap
detects NoUnmaskedPIIAtASink_MaskingCoversDirectPIIOnly
- pred MaskingCoversDirectPIIOnly {
-   all s: Sink, c: Column | (c in s.exposes and c in PIIColumn) implies c in s.masked
- }
+ pred MaskingCoversDirectPIIOnly {
+   all s: Sink, c: Column | (c in s.exposes and DerivedFromPII[c]) implies c in s.masked
+ }

harmless a comment on PIIColumn is reworded
- sig PIIColumn in Column {}  -- columns that directly hold PII, such as email or ssn
+ sig PIIColumn in Column {}  -- columns holding PII in the clear, e.g. email, ssn
